findings.claim:
"Stationary" is applied as a reading without its alternative.

The brief requires every reading to be labelled READING with both alternatives. Three places state the reading with no label and no alternative:
- proposal §3.1, line 152: '"Stationary" is read as: the state belongs to the position where it was taken; ... a move before it in the same window is allowed';
- proposal §8, line 502;
- H-AP §2, line 103: 'Also read, not asked'.

An obvious alternative would be: (b) the agent must not have moved earlier in the same window, so Move → Hide/Camouflage/Entrench is refused, which changes the combination matrix. The lane's other applied readings (no upkeep, §3.1; works lost on leaving, §4.3) do state their alternatives.

